# Gold light

When the user says **gold light** (or “apply gold light”) to a named card:

1. Use `GoldLight` from `@/components/branding/GoldLight`.
2. Parent card: `relative overflow-hidden group` (so hover works).
3. Put content in `relative z-10` above the light.
4. **Color:** default is gold `#F6A724`. When the user names a color, pass it as `color="#......"`.
5. Pass `active={selected}` (or equivalent) when the card has a selected state.

## Locked measurements (`GOLD_LIGHT`)

| Layer | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| Placement | Top **center** of the card (not top-left) |
| Wash height | `50%` of card |
| Ellipse | `108% × 144%` at `50% 0%` |
| Wash opacity | core `0.28` → mid `0.1` → fade |
| Hot spot | `8.4rem × 4.8rem`, centered on top border, `blur-md` |
| Rim | 1px top edge, brightest at center |

Tune only via `GOLD_LIGHT` / `GoldLight` so every instance stays in sync.

Do not confuse with **box grading** (dual navy+amber blobs) or **crimson** drag-row glow.
